[[Open This|How do I set/invalidate local user passwords?]]

---

https://docs.oxide.computer/guides/operator/faq#_how_do_i_setinvalidate_local_user_passwords

The ability to set or reset a password is available to users with the silo admin or fleet admin role via the local_idp_user_set_password API. The requester must provide the administrator with the specific user_id, which can be obtained using user_list or current_user_view.

To change the password for a given user, set the mode to password in the request body.

```json
// request.json
{
    "mode": "password",
    "value": "8kFf?,YP0ck#}'OE6QSQ"
}
```

To invalidate the password and revoke access, set the mode to login_disallowed in the request body instead:

```json
// request.json
{
    "mode": "login_disallowed"
}
```

Then run the following command:

```bash
oxide silo idp local user set-password --silo recovery --json-body request.json --user-id $SOME_USER
```
